# The words of the settings the scaffold declares in fs-starter, English (ADR 0057: MessageFormat 2). Every id needs a German twin in de.mf2.
setting-label-fs-rpc-single-ask = Ask before ending a silent program
setting-about-fs-rpc-single-ask = When a program of the same kind does not answer and could not be ended, ask first (wait, replace, abort). Without a window or terminal the program decides.
setting-label-fs-mcp-enabled = AI entry (local) open
setting-about-fs-mcp-enabled = Whether this machine's programs offer their local MCP entry. Off by default. This is no permission for an AI (that is a right); the vault is never reachable over MCP.
setting-label-fs-open-when-open = When something is already open
setting-about-fs-open-when-open = What happens when you open something that is already open in a window: ask first, switch to that window, open it as a tab (follows, not there before phase 2; until then it behaves like ask), or open another window.
setting-choice-fs-open-when-open-ask = Ask me
setting-choice-fs-open-when-open-switch = Switch to the open window
setting-choice-fs-open-when-open-tab = Open as a tab (follows)
setting-choice-fs-open-when-open-window = Open another window
